# Implementation Plan

Created March 1, 2026. This captures the phased plan for building the footballFrontEnd application. Priorities may shift — update this document as direction changes.

## Current State

### footballBackEnd (fully deployed and functional)
- AWS Lambda (Node.js 22.x) + API Gateway + RDS PostgreSQL
- 4 GET endpoints: `/players`, `/players/{id}`, `/players/{id}/stats`, `/players/{id}/roster-history`
- Cognito User Pool with Hosted UI, PKCE app client (no secret), authorization code flow
- API Gateway JWT authorizer validates **Cognito ID tokens** (not access tokens) against the app client ID
- Data loaded: 2023-2025 seasons, ~2,500 players, ~20,600 stat rows
- Daily sync Lambda via EventBridge + manual load/clear scripts
- 63 automated tests (37 unit + 26 integration) passing

### footballFrontEnd (early foundation)
- Next.js 16 with App Router, Tailwind v4, Vitest, Storybook
- Design system foundation: Button, Badge primitives with tests/stories
- Design tokens (brew/vegas palette, typography)
- TypeScript types for Player, League, Matchup
- No auth, no BFF routes, no data pages, no middleware

## Known Issue: ID Token vs. Access Token

The API Gateway JWT authorizer validates **ID tokens**, not access tokens. Cognito access tokens set the audience to the User Pool URL, but the authorizer checks against the **client ID**, which only matches ID tokens.

The BFF must send the **ID token** (not access token) as `Authorization: Bearer` to the AWS API. The `bff.mdc` code examples reference `session.accessToken` — this should be `session.idToken` when implementing.

## Phase 1: Auth + BFF Foundation (get the frontend talking to the backend)

Goal: A user can sign in via Cognito, and the frontend can fetch real player data from the AWS backend through the BFF proxy.

### 1.1 Environment setup
- [ ] Create `.env.local` with all required variables:
  - `AWS_API_BASE_URL=https://z8y6zlxrmc.execute-api.us-west-2.amazonaws.com`
  - `COGNITO_DOMAIN=https://football-dev.auth.us-west-2.amazoncognito.com`
  - `COGNITO_CLIENT_ID=12hi070g8mrjkefh1pciv624om`
  - `COGNITO_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/api/auth/callback`
  - `COGNITO_LOGOUT_URI=http://localhost:3000`
  - `SESSION_SECRET=<generate a 32+ char secret>`
- [ ] Create `.env.example` (no real values, just placeholder keys)
- [ ] Update `next.config.ts` if needed (image domains for ESPN headshots, etc.)

### 1.2 Install auth dependency
- [ ] `npm install iron-session`

### 1.3 Session management utilities
- [ ] Create `src/lib/session.ts` — iron-session configuration, `getSession`/`setSession`/`clearSession` helpers
- [ ] Session shape: `{ idToken: string, accessToken: string, refreshToken: string, expiresAt: number }`
- [ ] Remember: send **idToken** (not accessToken) to the AWS API Gateway

### 1.4 Auth route handlers
- [ ] `src/app/api/auth/login/route.ts` — PKCE verifier/challenge generation, redirect to Cognito Hosted UI
- [ ] `src/app/api/auth/callback/route.ts` — Exchange auth code for tokens, store in encrypted session cookie
- [ ] `src/app/api/auth/logout/route.ts` — Clear session cookie, redirect to Cognito logout
- [ ] `src/app/api/auth/session/route.ts` — Return current user info (decoded from ID token)

### 1.5 Route protection
- [ ] `src/middleware.ts` — Check for valid session cookie, redirect to login if missing on protected routes

### 1.6 Client-side auth hook
- [ ] `src/features/auth/useSession.ts` — Client hook that calls `/api/auth/session`, provides user state

### 1.7 BFF data proxy routes
- [ ] `src/app/api/players/route.ts` — Proxy GET to AWS `/players` with Bearer idToken
- [ ] `src/app/api/players/[id]/route.ts` — Proxy GET to AWS `/players/{id}`
- [ ] `src/app/api/players/[id]/stats/route.ts` — Proxy GET to AWS `/players/{id}/stats`
- [ ] `src/app/api/players/[id]/roster-history/route.ts` — Proxy GET to AWS `/players/{id}/roster-history`
- [ ] Token refresh: if idToken is expired, use refreshToken to get new tokens before proxying

### 1.8 API client
- [ ] `src/lib/api-client.ts` — Typed fetch wrapper for BFF endpoints (used by pages/features)

### 1.9 Verification
- [ ] Sign in through Cognito Hosted UI end-to-end
- [ ] Fetch player data through the BFF and see it rendered
- [ ] Verify token refresh works when idToken expires
- [ ] Verify unauthenticated access is rejected

