## Phase 4: Infrastructure Hardening

### 4.1 Security
- [ ] Remove `ALLOW_USER_PASSWORD_AUTH` from Cognito app client (keep SRP + refresh only)
- [ ] Add Vercel production URL to Cognito callback/logout URLs
- [ ] Align Lambda CORS headers with API Gateway (remove `*` wildcard)

### 4.2 Operations
- [ ] Replace bastion with SSM Session Manager
- [ ] Move DB password to AWS Secrets Manager
- [ ] Add CloudWatch alarms (Lambda errors, 5xx rates, RDS metrics)

### 4.3 CI/CD
- [ ] GitHub Actions or CodePipeline for backend (build + terraform apply)
- [ ] Vercel handles frontend deployment automatically

## Decision Log

| Date | Decision | Rationale |
|------|----------|-----------|
| 2026-03-01 | Send ID token (not access token) to AWS API | API Gateway JWT authorizer validates audience against client ID, which only matches in ID tokens |
| 2026-03-01 | Use iron-session for encrypted cookies | Documented in tech-stack.mdc and bff.mdc; keeps tokens server-side only |
| 2026-03-01 | Upgrade Lambda to Node.js 22.x | AWS ending Node 20 support April 30, 2026 |
| 2026-03-01 | Phase 1 focuses on auth + BFF patterns first | Frontend can't do anything useful without backend connectivity |
